{
 "section_summary": "This section contains wartime activity reports on Filipinos in Shanghai and Tientsin, compiled mainly from statements taken in 1945. They describe Japanese-sponsored associations, propaganda, allegiance ceremonies, travel to occupied China and the Philippines, and allegations that Filipino informants helped Japanese authorities arrest pro-American residents. The longer files on Vicente Casino and A. Y. Celis include competing accounts of their conduct.",
